<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Empirical knee-points increase smoothly with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta K</annotation></semantics></math> is well fitted by a linear function in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>,
confirming the additive correction <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> predicted by our robustness theorem.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Heavy-tailed Features</h3>

<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Heavy-tail stress test results (<math id="A5.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=200</annotation></semantics></math>).
Lower <math id="A5.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to heavier tails.
<math id="A5.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{nominal}}=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>nominal</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{nominal}}=64</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
