<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Empirical knee-points scale approximately as <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+c_{\rho})\cdot K_{\mathrm{nominal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>nominal</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+c_{\rho})\cdot K_{\mathrm{nominal}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
consistent with our dependence extension in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Extensions to Dependent Features ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Summary</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across all three stress tests,
the empirical knee-point increases smoothly with the violation strength,
either additively (drift), multiplicatively (tails), or by a dependence factor (temporal correlation).
These controlled experiments confirm that our non-asymptotic lower bound is
robust: violations of (A1) shift the threshold conservatively,
but do not invalidate the predictive power of <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> as a proxy for ICL stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Interpretability of the Proxy</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Predictive variance control via <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the design with rows <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x_{k})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x_{k})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}=\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}=\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>.
For ridge predictor
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}(x)=\phi(x)^{\top}\!\left(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\frac{\lambda}{K}I\right)^{\!-1}\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}(x)=\phi(x)^{\top}\!\left(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\frac{\lambda}{K}I\right)^{\!-1}\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y</annotation></semantics></math>,
if <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A6.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\widehat{f}(x_{\star})\mid\Phi\right)\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\delta+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\widehat{f}(x_{\star})\mid\Phi\right)\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\delta+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">See <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a> for details; it follows by the matrix inequality
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}(K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}(K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>
and the Rayleigh quotient bound <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}^{\top}A^{-1}\mathbf{v}\leq\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}^{\top}A^{-1}\mathbf{v}\leq\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theoretical link.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="Predictive variance control via 𝜆_min ‣ Appendix F Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> (Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>) shows that
a lower bound on <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>
suffices to control predictive variance of in-context regression,
providing a mechanistic rationale for why it correlates with stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Limitations.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">However, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> can be overly conservative in practice:
(i) tiny eigenvalues with negligible test alignment,
(ii) heavy tails beyond sub-Gaussian assumptions,
(iii) contextual dependence that alters effective conditioning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alternative surrogates.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We therefore also consider quantile eigenvalues <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the condition number <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, effective rank <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and average leverage scores.
These quantities often correlate more closely with empirical knee-points.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Calibration.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A light calibration step (estimating a global scale <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>
and quantile level <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> on a small validation set)
substantially improves predictive accuracy of the proxy
(see Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Measuring the Knee-Point ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Proof sketch of Proposition</h3>

<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the design matrix with rows <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x_{k})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x_{k})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and denote <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume the response obeys <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with homoscedastic noise
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.
Consider the ridge predictor</p>
<table id="A6.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x)~=~\phi(x)^{\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\cdot\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y\Bigr),\quad\lambda\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x)~=~\phi(x)^{\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\cdot\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y\Bigr),\quad\lambda\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For a fixed test point <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\star}:=\phi(x^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\star}:=\phi(x^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Linear form and conditional variance.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Conditioned on the design <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is linear in <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x^{\star})=a^{\top}y,\qquad a^{\top}=\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x^{\star})=a^{\top}y,\qquad a^{\top}=\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(y\mid\Phi)=\sigma^{2}I_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(y\mid\Phi)=\sigma^{2}I_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A6.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\|a\|_{2}^{2}~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\phi^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\|a\|_{2}^{2}~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\phi^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\,(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\,A^{-1}\phi^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\,(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\,A^{-1}\phi^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: matrix inequality.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\preceq A=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\preceq A=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{-1/2}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1/2}\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1/2}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1/2}\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</p>
<table id="A6.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Plugging into (<a href="#A6.E14" title="In Linear form and conditional variance. ‣ F.1 Proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A6.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Rayleigh quotient bound.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> and vector <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M^{-1}v\leq\|v\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M^{-1}v\leq\|v\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\phi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\phi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A6.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}~\leq~\frac{\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}~\leq~\frac{B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}~\leq~\frac{\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}~\leq~\frac{B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Combining with (<a href="#A6.E15" title="In Step 1: matrix inequality. ‣ F.1 Proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A6.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, whenever <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\hat{f}(x^{\star}))\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\delta+\lambda}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\hat{f}(x^{\star}))\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\delta+\lambda},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which establishes Proposition <a href="#A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="Predictive variance control via 𝜆_min ‣ Appendix F Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.
 <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) If <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the result still holds provided <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
(ii) For heteroscedastic noise, the bound uses the maximal variance.
(iii) Under model misspecification, bias terms can be separated, and the variance part remains controlled by <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Ablation Studies</h2>

<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overview.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To bridge the gap between theory and practice, we performed ten ablations that correspond to the key factors appearing in our formula and experimental pipeline. We first present a summary table that aggregates all results, followed by ten dedicated <span id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\subsection</span>s, each restating its own result with brief analysis and takeaway. All numbers are averages over multiple runs unless otherwise noted, and error ratios are defined as theoretical <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> divided by the empirical knee (lower is better).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>ratio Sensitivity</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Increasing <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math> reduces the theoretical upper bound from <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}\!\approx\!95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mn>95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}\!\approx\!95</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}\!\approx\!25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}\!\approx\!25</annotation></semantics></math>, with error ratio decreasing from <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.4\times</annotation></semantics></math>. The mechanism is through the effective spectral gap <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Numerically, <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> acts like a conservativeness amplifier. Theoretically, it encodes a robustness margin on <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Mathematically, it discounts the least eigenvalue to stabilize finite-sample estimation. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Correct scaling w.r.t. <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (using <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\rho\,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\rho\,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and pick an anchor <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A7.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}(\rho)=K^{*}(\rho_{0})\left(\frac{1-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho\,}\right)^{\!2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}(\rho)=K^{*}(\rho_{0})\left(\frac{1-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho\,}\right)^{\!2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For example, from <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.9</annotation></semantics></math> the factor is <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="81\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>81</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">81\times</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Effective Rank Definition</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Rank estimation method strongly affects tightness: thresholding gives <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math>, energy-based <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 2.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>2.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2.4\times</annotation></semantics></math>, and trace-based <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> The definition operationalizes model complexity. Threshold is safest but loosest; energy balances dominant and tail directions; trace emphasizes overall spread. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Rank definition</th>
<th id="A7.SS2.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS2.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Threshold</th>
<td id="A7.SS2.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS2.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Energy</th>
<td id="A7.SS2.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 2.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>2.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2.4\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS2.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Trace</th>
<td id="A7.SS2.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Sub-Gaussian Parameter</h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Increasing <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math> scales <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by several times, sometimes approaching an order-of-magnitude increase. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Numerically, <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a dominant driver of between-task variability. Theoretically, it reflects tail decay and concentration strength. Mathematically, it is the constant in sub-Gaussian concentration appearing in upper bounds. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS3.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><math id="A7.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A7.SS3.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Qualitative effect on <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS3.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.SS3.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">small</td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS3.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.SS3.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">several<math id="A7.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> larger</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Covariance Norm</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Using the spectral norm typically yields <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios, Frobenius yields <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math>, while mean-variance approximations can under-estimate and approach <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Spectral norm focuses on the hardest direction; Frobenius spreads mass across all directions; rough mean-variance may miss heavy directions and be overly optimistic. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Norm choice</th>
<th id="A7.SS4.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS4.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Spectral</th>
<td id="A7.SS4.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS4.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Frobenius</th>
<td id="A7.SS4.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS4.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Mean-variance</th>
<td id="A7.SS4.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1\times</annotation></semantics></math> (may under-estimate)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.5 </span>Label Tokenization</h3>

<div id="A7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Single-token labels (e.g., <span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">yes/no</span>, <span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">POS/NEG</span>) yield smaller knees and <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios, whereas multi-token labels (e.g., <span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">positive/negative</span>) often exceed <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Single-token labels shrink the effective output search space. Multi-token labels dilute probability mass and inflate the required <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Tokenization</th>
<th id="A7.SS5.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS5.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Single-token</th>
<td id="A7.SS5.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS5.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS5.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Multi-token</th>
<td id="A7.SS5.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\geq 3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 3\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.6 </span>Prompt Truncation Policy</h3>

<div id="A7.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> <em id="A7.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Latest-first</em> delivers smaller knees and <math id="A7.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios; <em id="A7.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">earliest-first</em> shifts the knee right and often exceeds <math id="A7.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math>; random truncation increases variance across runs. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Latest-first respects the model inductive bias toward local context; earliest-first tends to retain stale or less relevant examples; random adds sampling noise. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS6.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Policy</th>
<th id="A7.SS6.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS6.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS6.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Latest-first</th>
<td id="A7.SS6.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS6.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS6.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Earliest-first</th>
<td id="A7.SS6.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="&gt;3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;3\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS6.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS6.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Random</th>
<td id="A7.SS6.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">larger variance</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.7 </span>Theory Constant Scaling</h3>

<div id="A7.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> A global scale <math id="A7.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}_{\text{adj}}=C\cdot K^{*}_{\text{theory}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mtext>adj</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mtext>theory</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}_{\text{adj}}=C\cdot K^{*}_{\text{theory}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\approx 10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≈</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\approx 10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> systematically tightens predictions to <math id="A7.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Numerically, <math id="A7.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a cross-task calibrator. Theoretically, it compensates for conservative constants in concentration bounds. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS7.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><math id="A7.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A7.SS7.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Typical error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS7.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS7.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">∼</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.SS7.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS7.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS7.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.SS7.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> (uncalibrated)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.8 </span>Synthetic Data Experiments</h3>

<div id="A7.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Under controlled Gaussian features with known <math id="A7.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, the theory-to-practice gap shrinks to <math id="A7.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> This indicates that the larger gaps on real data primarily arise from violations of sub-Gaussian tails, linear separability, or spectral stability. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS8.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Setting</th>
<th id="A7.SS8.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS8.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS8.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Controlled Gaussian</th>
<td id="A7.SS8.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS8.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS8.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Real tasks</th>
<td id="A7.SS8.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.9 </span>Retrieval Strategy</h3>

<div id="A7.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Cosine-similarity nearest neighbor retrieval yields the smallest knees and <math id="A7.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios; random sampling degrades stability and often exceeds <math id="A7.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>; class-balanced sampling lies between. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Retrieval reshapes the empirical covariance around the test point, preserving a larger effective <math id="A7.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and tightening <math id="A7.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS9.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Retrieval</th>
<th id="A7.SS9.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS9.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS9.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Cosine-NN</th>
<td id="A7.SS9.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS9.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS9.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS9.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Balanced</th>
<td id="A7.SS9.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">intermediate</td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS9.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS9.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Random</th>
<td id="A7.SS9.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS9.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\geq 2.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2.5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.10 </span>Model Scale</h3>

<div id="A7.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> On SST-2, the empirical knee decreases from <math id="A7.SS10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 12</annotation></semantics></math> for a 124M model to <math id="A7.SS10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 7</annotation></semantics></math> for a 345M model, with the error ratio dropping from <math id="A7.SS10.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS10.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Larger models better exploit demonstrations and align more closely with theoretical assumptions (smaller effective noise, more stable spectra). 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS10.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A7.SS10.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.SS10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS10.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Model</th>
<th id="A7.SS10.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Knee (SST-2)</th>
<th id="A7.SS10.p1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.SS10.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS10.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">124M</th>
<td id="A7.SS10.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 12</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A7.SS10.p1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.SS10.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.SS10.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.SS10.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">345M</th>
<td id="A7.SS10.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A7.SS10.p1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A7.SS10.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Closing remarks.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across the ten axes, three levers consistently tighten the theory-to-practice gap: (i) increasing the effective spectral gap (via <math id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> choice, retrieval near the test point, and stable norm definitions), (ii) reducing effective noise (smaller <math id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, single-token labels, larger models), and (iii) cross-task calibration of conservative constants (<math id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-scaling). Under idealized assumptions validated by synthetic data, the gap nearly vanishes; on real tasks, careful choices along these levers reduce error ratios toward <math id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> while preserving reproducibility.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Theoretical Constants: Sources, Mappings, and Practical Calibration</h2>

<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>List of Constants and Quick Reference</h3>

<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A8.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ H.1 List of Constants and Quick Reference ‣ Appendix H Theoretical Constants: Sources, Mappings, and Practical Calibration ‣ Theoretical Bounds for Stable In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> summarizes all explicit or implicit constants, structural factors, and engineering fudge factors appearing in the paper. The following subsections provide:
(i) theoretical origins and geometric interpretations;
(ii) quantitative coupling with problem parameters (dimension <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, effective rank <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, signal-to-noise ratio, confidence level <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>);
(iii) a three-step experimental calibration guideline (simulation–calibration–cross-validation).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Constants and recommended values</figcaption>
<table id="A8.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A8.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
