</figure>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Theoretical Origins and Geometric Interpretation</h3>

<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Matrix Bernstein constants <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the sum of independent centered random matrices <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum Y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum Y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, Tropp (2012) shows</p>
<table id="A8.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\lambda_{\min}(S)\leq-t\right)\;\leq\;r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2v+\tfrac{2}{3}Rt}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\lambda_{\min}(S)\leq-t\right)\;\leq\;r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2v+\tfrac{2}{3}Rt}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The coefficients <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math> arise from the moment-generating-function method and are structural, non-adjustable constants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sub-Gaussian fourth-moment constant <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a mean-zero sub-Gaussian vector <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, an absolute constant <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures</p>
<table id="A8.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{4}\;\leq\;c_{1}\;\bigl(\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{2}\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{4}\;\leq\;c_{1}\;\bigl(\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{2}\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Examples:</p>
<ul id="A8.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gaussian: <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uniform on sphere: <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\approx 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\approx 3</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rademacher: <math id="A8.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\approx 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\approx 3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For anisotropic distributions, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> scales with the condition number <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(\Sigma)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\Sigma)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, after standardization and with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 50</annotation></semantics></math>, simulations suggest <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\in[1.5,6]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\in[1.5,6]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> recommended.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Covariance operator deviation constant <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Koltchinskii &amp; Lounici (2017, Thm. 3.1) proved</p>
<table id="A8.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\Sigma}-\Sigma\|\;\leq\;c_{2}\|\Sigma\|\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}}+\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\Sigma}-\Sigma\|\;\leq\;c_{2}\|\Sigma\|\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}}+\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Typical values:</p>
<ul id="A8.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A8.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sub-Gaussian: <math id="A8.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sub-exponential: <math id="A8.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=4</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finite fourth moment: <math id="A8.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> scales with kurtosis <math id="A8.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Empirically, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=3</annotation></semantics></math> suffices in 95% of cases for <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/n\in[0.1,0.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/n\in[0.1,0.5]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.3 </span>Coupling with Problem Parameters</h3>

<div id="A8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main sample-size requirement is</p>
<table id="A8.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\;\geq\;c^{\prime}\cdot r(\Sigma)\,\frac{t+\log d}{\varepsilon^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\;\geq\;c^{\prime}\cdot r(\Sigma)\,\frac{t+\log d}{\varepsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Implications:</p>
<ul id="A8.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A8.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A8.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> influences estimation error of the effective rank <math id="A8.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A8.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> scales the relative error <math id="A8.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> directly;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structural constants <math id="A8.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2,2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2,2/3</annotation></semantics></math> remain fixed;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Engineering factors <math id="A8.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime},c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime},c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> ensure practical safety, typically increasing with confidence level <math id="A8.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.4 </span>Three-Step Calibration Procedure</h3>

<div id="A8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A8.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A8.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A8.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulation calibration:</span> Generate synthetic Gaussian datasets across <math id="A8.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,n)</annotation></semantics></math> grids, estimate failure probabilities, and back out <math id="A8.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> with 95% quantile anchoring.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A8.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness to misspecification:</span> Test under sub-exponential, heavy-tailed, and real bootstrap data. If <math id="A8.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> inflates more than <math id="A8.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>, adjust by <math id="A8.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa/5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A8.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-validation locking of <math id="A8.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime},c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime},c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> On real data, run two-stage procedures with 5-fold cross-validation, plot error–sample size curves, and infer <math id="A8.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from the plateau point.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
